// recomp_seeds.json — this game's recompiler seeds (external/psxport/tools/recomp/emit.py --seeds).
//
// The recompiler discovers functions from the binary itself: the entry point, the pointer/table scans,
// then the direct-`jal` call graph. What it CANNOT see is anything reached only through a function
// pointer, or entered at a runtime-computed re-entry point, or an overlay's load base. Those are facts
// about THIS executable and THIS disc, so the framework ships none of them and every game supplies its
// own file. JSON with `//` comments; every key is optional.
//
// The executable seed sets are empty by measurement: the emitter independently roots traversal at
// the PS-EXE entry and discovers its direct-call graph. Add only runtime-observed fail-fast misses;
// duplicating the entry here would obscure the bootstrap contract instead of extending it.
//
// Two rules, both learned the hard way elsewhere in this workspace:
//
//   * NEVER copy another game's seed list. A foreign seed that lands inside your text SPLITS a real
//     function at an arbitrary offset — the emit SUCCEEDS and the recomp is silently corrupt.
//   * NEVER guess an overlay base. An overlay is keyed BY its load address, so a wrong base emits a
//     whole module of correctly-decoded instructions at wrong addresses, and every jal target,
//     pointer test and router lookup is then silently wrong. A missing base is a HARD ERROR in
//     emit.py, deliberately — that refusal is the feature.
//
// Grow it empirically: boot, and when the substrate fail-fasts with `[recomp-MISS] 0x800xxxxx`, add
// that address WITH a note on how it is reached. An address with no rationale is unreviewable later.
//
// This game has 21 .PRG images on the disc (BATTLE/TITLE/ENDING/INITBTL/SCREFF2 + 16 MENU/*), but
// MENU/MENUA.PRG is 0 bytes and therefore has no code or load base. tools/re_overlay.py verifies the
// other 20 individually from their own bytes (M2), then SHA-binds each owned image to rood-reverse
// before checking the reference link address (M3). Its --check-config gate compares this file and
// game_config.cpp back to the measurement; these values are not transcribed reference guesses.
{
  "main": [],
  "main_reentry": [],
  "overlay_bases": {
    "BATTLE": "0x80068800",
    "ENDING": "0x80068800",
    "INITBTL": "0x800F9800",
    "MAINMENU": "0x800F9800",
    "MENU0": "0x80102800",
    "MENU1": "0x80102800",
    "MENU2": "0x80102800",
    "MENU3": "0x80102800",
    "MENU4": "0x80102800",
    "MENU5": "0x80102800",
    "MENU7": "0x80102800",
    "MENU8": "0x80102800",
    "MENU9": "0x80102800",
    "MENUB": "0x80102800",
    "MENUC": "0x80102800",
    "MENUD": "0x80102800",
    "MENUE": "0x80102800",
    "MENUF": "0x80102800",
    "SCREFF2": "0x800F9800",
    "TITLE": "0x80068800"
  },
  "overlay_base_patterns": [],
  "overlay_seeds": {}
}
